# #112 — the surviving `*((&x) as *const T)` RAW-DUPLICATE population of stdlib.
#
# Format (tab- or space-separated, one row per SURVIVING occurrence):
#     <repo-relative file>   <symbol>   <ground-tag>   <refuse-fixture|->
#
# The population is DERIVED by tests/logos/stdlib_raw_dup_lint.sh from the tree
# (broad grep `\*\(\(&[^)]*\) as \*const `), not read from here. This file is the
# other half of a two-way agreement: a site in the tree that is not here reds, and a
# row here whose site is gone reds. The ground tags:
#
#   copy-bound    the enclosing impl carries `T: Copy`, so the bitwise duplicate can
#                 never see a droppable payload. The lint re-derives that bound from
#                 the impl header and requires a REFUSE fixture proving it bites.
#   rust-contract the duplicate is the declared semantics of the Rust API being
#                 shadowed, and the call is `unsafe` for exactly that reason.
#   bc-blocked    the duplicate LAUNDERS a borrow-checker over-refusal; deleting it
#                 makes the stdlib fail to build. UNSOUND for a droppable payload and
#                 must go the day the over-refusal closes.
#
# History: the census that opened #112 found 34 occurrences (the prompt's own narrow
# grep found 22 of them — it could not match a dotted receiver like `self.sep`). 29
# were closed by making the predicate/comparator surface BORROW, by moving values out
# with `mem::replace`, by `T: Clone`, or by deleting a gratuitous copy. These 5 remain.

stdlib/lang/iter/iter.logos    Iterator::reduce                bc-blocked      -
stdlib/lang/iter/iter.logos    ArrayChunksIter::next           copy-bound      tests/logos/fail/rawdup_array_chunks_copy_enforced_fail.expected
stdlib/lang/iter/iter.logos    MapWindowsIter::next            copy-bound      tests/logos/fail/rawdup_map_windows_copy_enforced_fail.expected
stdlib/lang/iter/iter.logos    RepeatNIter::next               copy-bound      tests/logos/fail/rawdup_repeat_n_copy_enforced_fail.expected
stdlib/mem/uninit/uninit.logos MaybeUninit::assume_init_read   rust-contract   -
